cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "ThermalAnalisys: open-source tool coupling deep learning detection of new buildings with intra-urban surface heat island analysis"
type: software
license: MIT
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.23632373
repository-code: "https://github.com/JoaoVictorNH/ThermalAnalisys"
abstract: >-
  Open-source tool, run through forms in Google Colab with Google Earth Engine,
  that couples a pre-trained multimodal Siamese U-Net detecting new buildings
  (10 m) from Sentinel-1 and Sentinel-2 imagery with an intra-urban surface
  urban heat island analysis from Landsat 8/9 surface temperature. It delivers
  a mask of new buildings with an accuracy benchmark against spectral index
  differencing, SUHI maps and classes relative to the urban perimeter, a 90 m
  indicator grid separating built, cleared and stable land, a test of the
  sensitivity of the thermal results to the acquisition dates, and GIS-ready
  rasters and tables.
keywords:
  - surface urban heat island
  - urban change detection
  - deep learning
  - land surface temperature
  - Google Earth Engine
  - semi-arid cities
  - urban planning
